/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    The same store, reached through an interface from inside another function.

    A method reached through an interface stands for every conforming object's version. (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Define interface keeper-of-rows for the void function keep, given (the series of number row).
Define object bag with (the series of series of number items) and keeper-of-rows.
Bind void to keep unto bag, given (the series of number s):
    Insert s into one's items.
Done.
Bind void to fill, given (the keeper-of-rows target, the series of number row):
    Cast target's keep on (row).
Done.
Define b as a new bag { the items (a series of series of number) }.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Cast fill on (b, inner).
Done.
State "done".
